3. Wording that ingested or adapted material must carry
=======================================================================

A record that reproduces or adapts third-party material must name the
source in its references[] and carry the source's licence. Use the
wording below for the sources that require it.

World Health Organization publications (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO)
  This is an adaptation of an original work: <Title>. Geneva: World
  Health Organization; <year>. Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO. This
  adaptation was not created by WHO. WHO is not responsible for the
  content or accuracy of this adaptation. The original edition shall be
  the binding and authentic edition.
  For a translation, replace "adaptation" with "translation". Do not use
  the WHO logo or suggest that WHO endorses VedaMD. VedaMD adaptations
  are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, as §4(b) of CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO allows.

